    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3845" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ar-vĕho</span></b> , exi, ectum, 3,
			v. a. (an old form for adveho, v. ad <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>init.</i>), <i>to
				bring</i>, <i>to procure</i> (only twice in
			Cato): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arvehant ligna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 138</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trapetum ubi arvectum erit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 135, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
